- op: discuss  # 0e7c
  at: '2026-08-18T05:08:41Z'  # 0e7c
  by: agent  # 0e7c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0e7c
  clock: 3  # 0e7c
  nonce: 0e7c  # 0e7c
  message: "DONE via PR #405 (dev 704b86df30). Behavioral evidence, measured on real data\nrather than fixtures.\n\nDRY RUN AGAINST THE ACTUAL 5.9 GB CACHE (40 live entries):\n  would soft-delete 987.9 MB (5 stale entries, cap 5.0 GB)\n  live after: 4.9 GB\n  projected archive cost at the measured ratio: ~59 MB\n\nEND-TO-END ON A SANDBOX COPY OF TWO REAL 200 MB ENTRIES (so the user's cache\nwas not mutated to prove the feature works):\n  reclaimed 201.1 MB in 1.1s\n  soft-deleted-surveys    1 zip   12.1 MB\n  soft-deleted-sketches   1 zip   84.1 KB\n  archives total 12.1 MB = 6.0% of what was reclaimed\n  RECOVERY: survey.json read back from the archive, 210,139,144 bytes,\n            BYTE-IDENTICAL to the original. Re-verified after the\n            cache_write_zip refactor, still byte-identical.\n\nTHE TWO DESIGN NUMBERS, priced before building rather than after:\n  compression   210.9 MB entry -> 12.7 MB in 1.0s (deflate-6, 6%, 16x). Paying\n                6% to make every eviction undoable is not a close call, and 1s\n                sits inside a run that already took minutes.\n  the split     survey.json is 1,259.9 MB of 1,264 MB across the six largest\n                entries (99.6%); sketch markdown + tier previews + handler\n                slices are 0.4%. That asymmetry is the whole reason for two\n                folders with independent caps.\n\nDEFAULTS: HYPERGUMBO_CACHE_MAX_GB=5.0 (0 disables),\nHYPERGUMBO_SOFT_DELETE_SURVEYS_GB=2.0, HYPERGUMBO_SOFT_DELETE_SKETCHES_GB=0.5.\nTHE HONEST CEILING IS 7.5 GB, NOT 5 -- the archives are part of the footprint\nand the spec says so.\n\nSCOPE EXPANSION, one item found and closed inside this PR: the fs-write\ndiscipline gate (test_runtime_fs_write_wrapper_discipline) fired on an in-memory\nZipFile, because it matches primitives by NAME and cannot tell a path-backed\nZipFile from a BytesIO one. It was right to fire. Fixed with wrappers rather\nthan an exemption -- cache_write_zip and cache_unlink now live in safety_zones\nwith the same enforced zone check cache_rmtree has, so archive writing and\narchive pruning cannot become the unsanitized host_fs flows the previous cycle\ndrove to 370 -> 0. Both wrappers have their own refuses-outside-the-zone tests.\n\nPOLICY: this reverses INV-padum's user-set 2026-05-17 \"no automatic eviction at\nany size\". The supersession is recorded on INV-padum in the owner's words;\nINV-padum keeps its satisfied status because the visibility work it delivered\nstill stands.\n\nNOT MEASURED: behaviour when two hypergumbo processes evict concurrently (the\n1-hour grace period and newest-per-repo protection make an in-flight entry the\nlast candidate, but no two-process test was run); and an archive larger than its\nfolder's whole cap, which would be zipped and then immediately pruned -- correct\nper the user's cap but wasteful, and it would take a ~33 GB entry at the\nmeasured ratio."  # 0e7c
